{"page": 1, "text": "Visible text of EX-99.1_2026-10-28_ex991-q32026.htm, sha256 2e6f9923900521b561fe7b6b80c8029f8edf3657185152ed4c0431af1e1a42e6.\nEX-99.1 2 ex991-q32026.htm EX-99.1\nInvestor Contact: Media Contact:\nGaren Sarafian Alexis Navratil\nir@bauschhealth.com corporate.communications@bauschhealth.com\n(877) 281-6642 (toll free) (848) 264-0934\nBAUSCH HEALTH ANNOUNCES THIRD QUARTER 2026 RESULTS, RAISES GUIDANCE\n\u2022Third Quarter Consolidated Revenues of $2.94 billion, up 10% on a Reported basis and 8% on an Organic1 basis over the prior year period \u2022GAAP Net Income Attributable to Bausch Health of $436 million and GAAP Net Income of $446 million \u2022GAAP Earnings per Diluted Share Attributable to Bausch Health of $1.15 compared to $0.48 in the prior year period; Adjusted Earnings per Diluted Share1 of $1.77 compared to $1.16 in the prior year period, an increase of 53% \u2022Consolidated Adjusted EBITDA Attributable to Bausch Health1 of $1,305 million, up 32% over the prior year period BAUSCH HEALTH EXCLUDING BAUSCH + LOMB THIRD QUARTER 2026 RESULTS\n\u2022Delivered fourteenth consecutive quarter of year-over-year Revenue and Adjusted EBITDA1 growth, with 12% Reported and 8% Organic Revenue1 growth and 32% Adjusted EBITDA1 growth \u2022Net Income increased $205 million over the prior year \u2022Generated $581 million in Cash Provided by Operating Activities and $539 million in Adjusted Cash Flows from Operations1 \u2022Raising full year 2026 Revenue, Adjusted EBITDA1, and Adjusted Cash Flows from Operations1 guidance\nLAVAL, QC, October 28, 2026 \u2013 Bausch Health Companies Inc. (NYSE:BHC)(TSX:BHC) (\"Bausch Health\" or the \"Company\" or \"we\" or \"our\") today announced its third quarter 2026 financial results and other key updates from the quarter.\n\"Bausch Health, excluding Bausch + Lomb, delivered another solid quarter, marking fourteen consecutive quarters of year-over-year Revenue and Adjusted EBITDA growth. We also achieved an important milestone, with quarterly Adjusted EBITDA, excluding Bausch + Lomb, exceeding $1 billion for the first time. Our performance reflects disciplined execution across the portfolio, with healthy cash generation supporting more than $500 million of net debt reduction during the quarter. These results give us confidence to again raise our full year 2026 guidance. We remain focused on operational excellence, sustainable growth, and long-term value creation,\" said Thomas J. Appio, Chief Executive Officer, Bausch Health.\nThe Company also announced that its Board of Directors has authorized a $50 million share repurchase program, with the primary objective of offsetting dilution associated with the anticipated vesting of management equity awards in 2027.\nThird Quarter 2026 Revenue Performance\n"}
{"page": 2, "text": "Total consolidated reported revenues were $2.94 billion for the third quarter of 2026, compared with $2.68 billion in the third quarter of 2025, an increase of $260 million, or 10%. Excluding the impact of acquisitions of $37 million and divestitures and discontinuations of $11 million, revenue increased 8% on an organic1 basis compared with the third quarter of 2025. The net impact of foreign exchange was de minimis in the quarter.\n___________________________________ 1 This is a non-GAAP measure or a non-GAAP ratio. For further information on non-GAAP measures and non-GAAP ratios, please refer to the \"Non-GAAP Information\" section of this news release. Please also refer to tables at the end of this news release for a reconciliation of this and other non-GAAP measures and ratios to the most directly comparable GAAP measure.\n1 | Page\nReported revenues by segment were as follows:\nThree Months Ended\nSeptember 30, Reported Change Change at Constant Currency1 Change in Organic Revenue1\n(in millions) 2026 2025 Amount Pct.\nTotal Bausch Health Revenues $2,941 $2,681 $260 10 % 10 % 8 %\nBausch Health (excl. B+L)1 $1,566 $1,400 $166 12 % 11 % 8 %\nSalix segment $831 $716 $115 16 % 16 % 14 %\nInternational segment $299 $286 $13 5 % 3 % 4 %\nSolta Medical segment $165 $140 $25 18 % 16 % (4 %)\nDiversified segment $271 $258 $13 5 % 5 % 5 %\nBausch + Lomb segment $1,375 $1,281 $94 7 % 8 % 7 %\nSalix Segment Salix segment reported revenues were $831 million for the third quarter of 2026, compared with $716 million for the third quarter of 2025, an increase of $115 million, or 16%. Segment revenues increased 14% on an organic1 basis compared with the third quarter of 2025. Xifaxan\u00ae was the primary contributor to growth, with 16% revenue growth in the third quarter of 2026.\nInternational Segment International segment reported revenues were $299 million for the third quarter of 2026, compared with $286 million for the third quarter of 2025, an increase of $13 million, or 5%. Excluding the impact of foreign exchange of $4 million, segment revenues grew 4% on an organic1 basis compared with the third quarter of 2025, led by Canada.\nSolta Medical Segment Solta Medical segment reported revenues were $165 million for the third quarter of 2026, compared with $140 million in the third quarter of 2025, an increase of $25 million, or 18% aided by the acquisition of our full service distributor in China. Excluding a $2 million favorable impact from foreign exchange and acquisitions of $29 million, segment revenues decreased by 4% on an organic1 basis compared with the third quarter of 2025 with the Asia Pacific region decreasing modestly.\n"}
{"page": 3, "text": "Diversified Segment Diversified segment reported revenues were $271 million for the third quarter of 2026, compared with $258 million for the third quarter of 2025, an increase of $13 million, or 5%. Segment revenues increased 5% on an organic1 basis compared with the third quarter of 2025. The increase in organic1 revenue was primarily driven by double-digit growth in Dermatology.\nBausch + Lomb Segment Bausch + Lomb segment reported revenues were $1.38 billion for the third quarter of 2026, compared with $1.28 billion for the third quarter of 2025, an increase of $94 million, or 7%. Excluding the impact of foreign exchange of $6 million, acquisitions of $8 million and divestitures and discontinuations of $2 million, segment revenues increased 7% on an organic1 basis compared with the third quarter of 2025.\n2 | Page\nConsolidated Operating Income Consolidated operating income was $983 million for the third quarter of 2026, compared with consolidated operating income of $619 million for the third quarter of 2025, an increase of $364 million.\nConsolidated Net Income Attributable to Bausch Health Consolidated net income attributable to Bausch Health for the third quarter of 2026 was $436 million, compared with consolidated net income attributable to Bausch Health of $179 million for the third quarter of 2025.\nConsolidated Adjusted Net Income Attributable to Bausch Health1 Consolidated adjusted net income attributable to Bausch Health1 for the third quarter of 2026 was $673 million, compared with $434 million for the third quarter of 2025, an increase of $239 million.\nConsolidated Earnings Per Share Attributable to Bausch Health Consolidated earnings per share attributable to Bausch Health for the third quarter of 2026 was $1.15 on a diluted basis, compared with consolidated earnings per share of $0.48 on a diluted basis for the third quarter of 2025.\nConsolidated Adjusted Earnings Per Share Attributable to Bausch Health1 Consolidated adjusted earnings per share attributable to Bausch Health1 for the third quarter of 2026 was $1.77, compared with $1.16 for the third quarter of 2025.\nConsolidated Adjusted EBITDA Attributable to Bausch Health1 Consolidated adjusted EBITDA attributable to Bausch Health1 was $1,305 million for the third quarter of 2026, compared with $986 million for the third quarter of 2025, an increase of $319 million.\nConsolidated Cash Provided by Operating Activities The Company generated $813 million of cash from operating activities in the third quarter of 2026, an increase of 101% versus $405 million in the third quarter of 2025.\nBalance Sheet Highlights As of September 30, 2026, Bausch Health reported consolidated cash and cash equivalents of $2,485 million, up from $1,309 million as of December 31, 2025. The Company remains focused on strengthening its balance sheet and delivering value to all stakeholders.\nFocus on Strategic Priorities\n"}
{"page": 4, "text": "The Company exits the third quarter of 2026 with strong financial momentum, with revenue and earnings growth across multiple segments. Upon the successful completion of major refinancing initiatives in the prior twelve-month period, the Company materially improved its debt maturity profile. The Company remains committed to evaluating all options for unlocking shareholder value, including maximizing the value of our Bausch Health and Bausch + Lomb assets.\n3 | Page\n2026 Financial Outlook\nThe Company updated its Consolidated full year Revenue and Adjusted EBITDA1 guidance for 2026.\nBausch Health (excluding Bausch + Lomb) is raising its full year Revenue, Adjusted EBITDA1, and Adjusted Cash Flows from Operations1 guidance, which includes the currently estimated impact of applicable tariffs for the calendar year as of the date of this release.\nCurrent Guidance (as of October 28, 2026)\nBHC BHC\n(excl. B+L) B+L\nRevenues (in billions) $10.975 - $11.175 $5.525 - $5.625 $5.450 - $5.550\nRevenue growth vs. Prior Year 7% - 9%\nAdjusted EBITDA1 (in billions) $4.315 - $4.415 $3.225 - $3.275 $1.090 - $1.140\nAdj. EBITDA1 growth vs. Prior Year 12% - 14%\nAdjusted Cash Flows from Operations1 (in billions) $1.600 - $1.675\n"}
{"page": 5, "text": "Other than with respect to GAAP revenues, the Company only provides guidance on a non-GAAP basis. The Company does not provide a reconciliation of forward-looking Adjusted EBITDA1 to GAAP net income (loss) or forward-looking Adjusted Cash Flows from Operations1 to GAAP cash provided by operating activities, due to the inherent difficulty in forecasting and quantifying certain amounts that are necessary for such reconciliation. Because deductions (such as restructuring, gain or loss on extinguishment of debt and litigation and other matters) used to calculate projected net income (loss) and payments (such as payments of legal settlements, transformation costs, separation costs and separation-related costs, interest charged against premium, financing fees paid in connection with the debt refinancing transactions and acquired IPR&D expense) used to calculate Adjusted Cash Flows from Operations1 vary dramatically based on actual events, the Company is not able to forecast on a GAAP basis with reasonable certainty all adjustments needed in order to provide a GAAP calculation of projected net income (loss) or cash provided by operating activities at this time. The amount of these adjustments may be material and, therefore, could result in projected GAAP net income (loss) being materially less than projected Adjusted EBITDA1. These statements represent forward-looking information and may represent a financial outlook, and actual results may vary. Please see the risks and assumptions referred to in the \u201cForward-looking Statements\u201d section of this news release. The guidance in this news release is only effective as of the date it is given and will not be updated or affirmed unless and until the Company publicly announces updated or affirmed guidance. The rapid recent developments in the evolving landscape of tariffs and responses have resulted in uncertainty regarding these measures and the effects they may have. We continue to assess the direct and indirect impacts on our businesses of such tariffs, including retaliatory tariffs and other trade protectionist measures as the situation develops, and there can be no assurance that such impacts will not be adverse.\n4 | Page\nConference Call Details\nDate: Wednesday, October 28, 2026\nTime: 5:00 p.m. EDT\nWebcast: http://ir.bauschhealth.com/events-and-presentations\nA replay of the conference call will be available on the investor relations website.\n"}
{"page": 6, "text": "About Bausch Health Bausch Health Companies Inc. (NYSE:BHC)(TSX:BHC) is a global, diversified pharmaceutical company enriching lives through our relentless drive to deliver better health care outcomes. We develop, manufacture and market a range of products primarily in gastroenterology, hepatology, neuroscience, dermatology, dentistry, aesthetics, international pharmaceuticals and eye health, through our controlling interest in Bausch + Lomb Corporation. Our ambition is to be a globally integrated healthcare company, trusted and valued by patients, HCPs, employees and investors. For more information about Bausch Health, visit www.bauschhealth.com and connect with us on LinkedIn.\n"}
